```cs
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

//...

[Test]
public void AssertTest()
{
    MatchCollection matches = Regex.Matches(text, @"\bDebug\.Assert\(.*?\);");

    foreach (Match match in matches)
    {
        Console.WriteLine(match.Value);
    }
}
```
This will output all the assert statements from your test code. But please note that the actual parsing of the code is complex problem (you can't just dump code into a regex, not all regexes can match the grammar of C#). This is why the code above will only find statements that look like they might be `Debug.Assert(...)`. It is a more comprehensive approach but with more complexity.

